  {
   "where": "main/4",
   "type": "Title",
   "value": "🪣 Understand Materials with the Tank Analogy",
   "key": null,
   "help": "",
   "proto": {
    "tag": "h1",
    "body": "🪣 Understand Materials with the Tank Analogy"
   }
  },
  {
   "where": "main/5",
   "type": "Expander",
   "container": true,
   "proto": {
    "label": "🧠 What does this tool show?",
    "expanded": false
   }
  },
  {
   "where": "main/5/0",
   "type": "Markdown",
   "value": "This tool shows how a **single electrode material** behaves inside a battery,\nusing the **tank analogy**.  \n\n- Think of the material as a tank that can be filled with lithium, just like\nfilling water into a container.  \n- The **curve shape** of the tank tells us how much lithium fits at each \"height\".  \n- The **steep parts** of the curve (big dQ/dV) mean the material can take in a lot\nof lithium without much change in voltage, like a wide part of the tank.  \n- The **flat parts** mean even a small amount of lithium changes the voltage a lot,\nlike a narrow neck of the tank.  \n\nOn the left, you see the **tank view** (dQ/dV). On the right, you see how the\n**voltage changes** as the tank fills (the OCV curve). Observe, how peaks in the dQ/dV reflect as plateaus in the OCV curve.\n\nBy moving the slider (SoC), you can explore how the lithium filling level relates\nto both views at the same time.",
   "key": null,
   "help": "",
   "proto": {
    "body": "This tool shows how a **single electrode material** behaves inside a battery,\nusing the **tank analogy**.  \n\n- Think of the material as a tank that can be filled with lithium, just like\nfilling water into a container.  \n- The **curve shape** of the tank tells us how much lithium fits at each \"height\".  \n- The **steep parts** of the curve (big dQ/dV) mean the material can take in a lot\nof lithium without much change in voltage, like a wide part of the tank.  \n- The **flat parts** mean even a small amount of lithium changes the voltage a lot,\nlike a narrow neck of the tank.  \n\nOn the left, you see the **tank view** (dQ/dV). On the right, you see how the\n**voltage changes** as the tank fills (the OCV curve). Observe, how peaks in the dQ/dV reflect as plateaus in the OCV curve.\n\nBy moving the slider (SoC), you can explore how the lithium filling level relates\nto both views at the same time.",
    "element_type": "NATIVE"
   }
  },
